2502.13228v2
We introduce a novel formulation that recasts conformal prediction in the framework of Bayesian quadrature, yielding data-conditional, distribution-free risk guarantees that are both interpretable and tight. The paper highlights a marked improvement over traditional frequentist approaches by leveraging Bayesian integration techniques to directly model the expected loss profile of a predictor. Extensive experimental evaluations on high-stakes prediction tasks demonstrate that the proposed method not only maintains reliable coverage but also produces significantly tighter risk bounds. Empirical results include thorough benchmark comparisons, sensitivity analyses regarding the choice of quadrature design points, and robustness studies under model misspecification—confirming that the Bayesian quadrature formulation consistently outperforms standard conformal methods in both reliability and computational efficiency.
``` 
